\cf2 Over the days, Janine moved the injections between muscle groups and adjusted the dose against what the blood work told her. Each morning she smuggled another tube of Pin Cushion\'92s blood into HIBReLabs. Each evening she brought the results home on a thumb drive and projected them into the air in her study.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Pin Cushion developed strong preferences about injection sites. \'93My left thigh is cancelled.\'94\
\'93It isn\'92t. The bruising has already gone, see?\'94\
Pin Cushion looked close at her thigh. \'93I\'92m unfollowing it,\'94 she said as she made a baroque sweep across her tablet.\
\'93Then you won\'92t be feeling this.\'94 Janine used the left thigh anyway.\
The next day, Janine noticed Pin Cushion getting off the couch without pushing off her knees. Pin Cushion didn\'92t seem to be aware of it. That evening, Janine had the last three sets of results hanging together above the holoscreen when Pin Cushion wandered into the study.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \'93What are you looking at?\'94\
\'93You.\'94\
Pin Cushion came around the desk. \'93Am I winning?\'94\
Janine pulled the latest results to the front. \'93It looks that way.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 A few days later Pin Cushion climbed the stairs holding only one rail. Then she forgot to hold that one. Janine watched from the bottom.\
The exercise bike remained an enemy, but mostly just on principle. Certain pieces of sporting equipment deserved no forgiveness, even on the evening that Pin Cushion easily pedalled past two kilometres. Then three. Her right hip wasn\'92t putting compensating effort into her thigh movement. She turned the resistance up herself.\
Janine kept her eyes on her tablet.\
\'93You can watch now,\'94 Pin Cushion said.\
Janine looked up.\
\'93Just don\'92t get weird.\'94\
\'93I won\'92t.\'94\
\'93You\'92re already weird.\'94 Pin Cushion kept pedalling.
